  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 238 PM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nDeep troughing will settle just north of the Great Lakes with low-\namplitude ridging sitting across the Great Basin. This will promote \nnorthwesterly flow. The combination of westerly downsloping winds \nand the proximity to a thermal ridge nosing in from the southwest \nwill lead to a mild and dry pattern through the forecast period. In \nfact, morning EPS/GEFS guidance show < 10% potential that any point \nin the local area sees a tenth of an inch or more moisture through \nDay 9 (Saturday). A pattern change towards that Day 8-10 range \nshould lead to increasing moisture quality as ridging breaks down \nover the west and a more southwesterly pattern sets up. A fairly \nactive northern stream jet should allow for multiple disturbances to \ncross the region, including frontal boundaries which may lead to \nmore variable temperatures, but confidence in precise timing remains \nlow. This is illustrated well with fairly consistent inner-quartile \nMaxT values in NBM data for Tuesday through Saturday before a large \nchange occurs on Sunday with significant spread in 25th and 75th \npercentile values.",
